{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-96063","model_call":10,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ maps classroom teaching benefits)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ maps classroom teaching benefits)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_1002533346#8_2137813519","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3057","rank":1,"snippet":"January 10, 2020 Why mind mapping works: the benefits of mind mapping Radiant thinking: mind maps explained Memory Creativity Learning<cover>Teaching Planning and organization Presenting Problem-solving How to harness the benefits mind mapping References \" , \"segment\": \"Because they encourage the brain to make associations between different keywords, phrases and images, they can be used by students to brainstorm ideas for creative projects (either alone or within a group), as well as help them to plan and structure work such as essays, reports and presentations. Mind maps are also a great revision aid due to the fact that they can be used to break down complex information and improve memorization and recall. Goodnough and Woods (2002)6 discovered that students perceived using the technique as a fun, interesting and motivating approach to learning. Several students attributed the fun aspect to the opportunity to be creative when creating maps through a variety of choices in color, symbols, keywords, and design. Mind mapping has been shown to bring a renewed sense of enthusiasm to the classroom </cover>because it increases student confidence and sense of skill in mastering assigned materials (Mento et al, 1999)7. Teaching As a "},"time":320},"model_calls":10,"document_judgments":4,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
